This directory contains a copy of the Corrosion project.

  - URL: https://github.com/corrosion-rs/corrosion.git
  - Commit: 56a1ed11ad7841255048659024363cd0fade31f4

The simplest way of updating its contents is to re-create the directory
from scratch, and restoring the needed files with Git. Example commands:

  rm -rf Source/ThirdParty/corrosion/*
  cp -ar ../path/to/corrosion/* Source/ThirdParty/corrosion/
  git checkout -- \
      Source/ThirdParty/corrosion/README.WebKit
  rm -fr Source/ThirdParty/corrosion/test

Then check whether the updated sources require any changes to the CMake build system, and update the
git commit identifier and tag in this file.
